      "id": 1,
      "text": "McKenney sits on a former railroad mainline that once carried the Richmond, Petersburg and Carolina Railroad, completed in 1900.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McKenney%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The line, later called the S‑line, ran until the 1980s before CSX abandoned the Norlina Subdivision, leaving McKenney isolated.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McKenney%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Three sites in the area—Montrose, the Sappony Church, and Zehmer Farm—are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
